WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.011
- Hello everyone.

00:00:01.011 --> 00:00:03.809
So, welcome to another
episode of Unlocking Lily.

00:00:03.809 --> 00:00:06.745
So, it's always been my
dream to be a speaker,

00:00:06.745 --> 00:00:08.813
which lead me to quit my day job

00:00:08.813 --> 00:00:10.818
to pursue this full time.

00:00:10.818 --> 00:00:14.744
And all of you are coming
along for this journey with me.

00:00:14.744 --> 00:00:17.827
(loud explosion effect)

00:00:17.827 --> 00:00:20.476
So, in every episode I
take a different challenge

00:00:20.476 --> 00:00:22.599
to really help me grow as a speaker.

00:00:22.599 --> 00:00:24.681
So, in this video I'm going to be filming

00:00:24.681 --> 00:00:26.086
at Yonge-Dundas Square,

00:00:26.086 --> 00:00:28.797
the busiest intersection in Toronto.

00:00:28.797 --> 00:00:30.937
Because I learned from Brené Brown

00:00:30.937 --> 00:00:34.126
that if there's something
meaningful that I want to do,

00:00:34.126 --> 00:00:37.016
I need to have the courage to show up.

00:00:37.016 --> 00:00:38.758
If I want to be a successful speaker,

00:00:38.758 --> 00:00:42.586
I need to be able to
deliver my speech whenever,

00:00:42.586 --> 00:00:44.976
wherever, in front of whoever.

00:00:44.976 --> 00:00:46.340
So wish me luck

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:49.184
and hope everything goes well (laughs).

00:00:49.184 --> 00:00:51.634
All right, so today's the
day I'm going to be filming

00:00:51.634 --> 00:00:53.432
at Yonge-Dundas Square.

00:00:53.432 --> 00:00:56.418
To be honest with you, I
think leading up to it,

00:00:56.418 --> 00:00:57.707
I felt so nervous even like
a month ago when I thought

00:00:57.707 --> 00:00:58.990
about this idea.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:02.211
People staring at me is going to be such

00:01:02.211 --> 00:01:05.207
an anxiety-provoking experience,

00:01:05.207 --> 00:01:07.408
but I actually feel really good.

00:01:07.408 --> 00:01:09.404
I feel more excited than anything else.

00:01:09.404 --> 00:01:10.882
I don't know.

00:01:10.882 --> 00:01:11.888
I don't know what it is.

00:01:11.888 --> 00:01:13.341
Maybe it's just thinking
about it over and over again,

00:01:13.341 --> 00:01:17.277
or it could be I have been
practicing more and more

00:01:17.277 --> 00:01:18.950
in the last month.

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:20.408
I don't know, but you know,

00:01:20.408 --> 00:01:23.066
I'm right here at my house.

00:01:23.066 --> 00:01:25.230
Things could be very
different when I get there,

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:26.966
so we'll see how it goes.

00:01:26.966 --> 00:01:28.794
So we locked up our house.

00:01:28.794 --> 00:01:31.171
My lovely husband is going to.

00:01:31.171 --> 00:01:32.545
Look at your hair!
(man laughs)

00:01:32.545 --> 00:01:34.006
- Wow.
- Oh my goodness!

00:01:34.006 --> 00:01:35.421
- Looks like (mutters).
- That is like, man bun

00:01:35.421 --> 00:01:36.667
to the max!
(man laughs)

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:39.009
Anyway (laughs).

00:01:39.009 --> 00:01:41.985
He's going to drive me to the Go Station.

00:01:41.985 --> 00:01:43.439
I'm going to take the Go Train

00:01:43.439 --> 00:01:45.407
to downtown Toronto.

00:01:45.407 --> 00:01:47.450
Oh, look at that hair!

00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:48.456
- Yeah, she thinks she's all tough, eh,

00:01:48.456 --> 00:01:49.982
but wait 'til I drop her
off at the Go Station.

00:01:49.982 --> 00:01:51.365
She's going to start.
- What?

00:01:51.365 --> 00:01:52.605
- She's going to start
quaking in her booties.

00:01:52.605 --> 00:01:53.779
- Oh yeah, okay.

00:01:53.779 --> 00:01:54.793
We'll see, we'll see.

00:01:54.793 --> 00:01:57.376
(upbeat music)

00:02:01.811 --> 00:02:04.228
I didn't realize I actually
missed the last train.

00:02:04.228 --> 00:02:06.160
I came to the station a little too late.

00:02:06.160 --> 00:02:08.802
It's either the trains run
really early in the morning,

00:02:08.802 --> 00:02:13.130
like around 5:00 AM or
really late in the afternoon,

00:02:13.130 --> 00:02:14.953
so I'm going to be taking the bus.

00:02:14.953 --> 00:02:17.146
I hope I'm standing in the right spot.

00:02:17.146 --> 00:02:20.854
I had some lovely gentlemen over there

00:02:20.854 --> 00:02:24.079
in the Blue Jay shirt that pointed me

00:02:24.079 --> 00:02:25.294
in the right direction.

00:02:25.294 --> 00:02:26.450
Yeah.

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:27.490
So I have a new friend
here that helped me out

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:28.329
- Hi.
- In pointing me

00:02:28.329 --> 00:02:30.014
in the right direction.

00:02:30.014 --> 00:02:30.847
What's your name?

00:02:30.847 --> 00:02:31.680
- Hi there.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:32.513
I'm Greg and I'm from Beri and heading out

00:02:32.513 --> 00:02:33.614
to the Blue Jay Games.

00:02:33.614 --> 00:02:34.622
- Yes.
- And Lily tells me

00:02:34.622 --> 00:02:35.999
that today, she's going
to try to face her fears.

00:02:35.999 --> 00:02:38.897
That's what this episode's about
and it's about facing fears

00:02:38.897 --> 00:02:41.645
and she's going ride the
route filming in public.

00:02:41.645 --> 00:02:42.653
This is going to be your big thing.

00:02:42.653 --> 00:02:43.670
- Yes, yes.
- So that's pretty cool.

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:44.929
That's exciting.
- Do you have a fear?

00:02:44.929 --> 00:02:46.359
- I don't.
- Oh!

00:02:46.359 --> 00:02:47.436
- I don't have any
fears that I know about.

00:02:47.436 --> 00:02:48.473
- Fearless.
- Nothing, yeah.

00:02:48.473 --> 00:02:49.487
I'm not fearless, I'm sure.

00:02:49.487 --> 00:02:54.143
You know, there's always the
fear of not being successful

00:02:54.143 --> 00:02:54.976
or not taking care of your family.

00:02:54.976 --> 00:02:56.223
Those are always the common ones,

00:02:56.223 --> 00:02:57.569
but other than that, no.

00:02:57.569 --> 00:02:58.856
Nothing really.

00:02:58.856 --> 00:02:59.881
- Awesome.
- It's just one

00:02:59.881 --> 00:03:00.887
of those things.
- All right,

00:03:00.887 --> 00:03:01.720
you just push to rid the fear.

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:02.553
- (laughs) I do, yeah.

00:03:02.553 --> 00:03:03.386
- Right?
- Yeah, you just learn to cope

00:03:03.386 --> 00:03:04.219
and you learn to death with it, yeah.

00:03:04.219 --> 00:03:05.052
- All right, well, thank you so much.

00:03:05.052 --> 00:03:06.020
- No problem.
- Thank you.

00:03:06.020 --> 00:03:07.023
- I got to another station
and I'm supposed to take

00:03:07.023 --> 00:03:08.856
another bus from here.

00:03:09.942 --> 00:03:10.935
It was interesting.

00:03:10.935 --> 00:03:14.139
I got to meet a gentleman named Greg

00:03:14.139 --> 00:03:16.884
and after he did the
video, we started talking

00:03:16.884 --> 00:03:19.822
and he said that he's
into leadership stuff too

00:03:19.822 --> 00:03:24.435
and how he guides his employees
to become better leaders.

00:03:24.435 --> 00:03:27.342
I never used to approach strangers.

00:03:27.342 --> 00:03:29.744
It's something that I had another fear of,

00:03:29.744 --> 00:03:31.996
but you know, sometimes
approaching strangers,

00:03:31.996 --> 00:03:33.005
you never know.

00:03:33.005 --> 00:03:34.522
You could learn a lot from them.

00:03:34.522 --> 00:03:35.355
Yeah, so.

00:03:36.552 --> 00:03:38.327
Something good came out of it.

00:03:38.327 --> 00:03:42.508
All right guys, so I'm
finally here, downtown.

00:03:42.508 --> 00:03:44.254
It took a long time.

00:03:44.254 --> 00:03:46.414
I was on the bus for about
two-and-a-half hours.

00:03:46.414 --> 00:03:47.710
I'm actually really hungry.

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:51.145
I'm going to go find something to eat

00:03:51.145 --> 00:03:55.621
and then take another subway
after Yonge-Dundas Square,

00:03:55.621 --> 00:03:58.012
so I'm actually, for those
of you who don't know

00:03:58.012 --> 00:04:00.496
downtown Toronto, I'm really south

00:04:00.496 --> 00:04:03.957
and Yonge-Dundas is about
20 minutes from here,

00:04:03.957 --> 00:04:05.656
but I'm going to go grab some food

00:04:05.656 --> 00:04:07.272
and go to the bathroom too.

00:04:07.272 --> 00:04:09.439
Actually, that's too much (laughs),

00:04:09.439 --> 00:04:10.616
but I got to go.

00:04:10.616 --> 00:04:13.199
(upbeat music)

00:04:19.046 --> 00:04:21.278
Well, I found a washroom
and I got my food,

00:04:21.278 --> 00:04:24.017
so I'm going to try to find

00:04:24.017 --> 00:04:25.641
somewhere that I can
sit and eat before I do

00:04:25.641 --> 00:04:28.983
my big filming at Yonge-Dundas Square.

00:04:28.983 --> 00:04:30.194
Yeah.

00:04:30.194 --> 00:04:34.042
So I finally got to Yonge-Dundas Square

00:04:34.042 --> 00:04:35.985
and I realize that I messed up.

00:04:35.985 --> 00:04:36.985
I forgot my,

00:04:38.628 --> 00:04:40.545
I forgot my big tripod.

00:04:41.812 --> 00:04:44.758
I don't know, I left
it in my husband's car.

00:04:44.758 --> 00:04:48.525
So I have my little one that Nina gave me,

00:04:48.525 --> 00:04:49.987
so I'm going to try to use that.

00:04:49.987 --> 00:04:51.714
Also another thing is,

00:04:51.714 --> 00:04:54.047
I got here and there's like,

00:04:55.026 --> 00:04:57.153
I mean, there are people here,

00:04:57.153 --> 00:04:59.849
but it's nowhere close to as busy

00:04:59.849 --> 00:05:01.432
as I was expecting,

00:05:02.966 --> 00:05:04.299
so I don't know.

00:05:05.198 --> 00:05:06.299
I don't know.

00:05:06.299 --> 00:05:08.450
I'm thinking maybe I should
find a busier place downtown

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:09.737
to film because really,

00:05:09.737 --> 00:05:11.788
I think there's about,

00:05:11.788 --> 00:05:15.657
I don't even know, maybe 50 people around.

00:05:15.657 --> 00:05:19.155
I was expecting hundreds,
maybe even 1,000,

00:05:19.155 --> 00:05:20.770
but not a lot of people.

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:21.767
I don't know what's going on.

00:05:21.767 --> 00:05:25.278
It's a Friday afternoon at Yonge-Dundas

00:05:25.278 --> 00:05:26.835
and there's no one around.

00:05:26.835 --> 00:05:28.253
Interesting.

00:05:28.253 --> 00:05:31.003
Anyway, I'll try to figure it out

00:05:31.934 --> 00:05:33.377
and yeah.

00:05:33.377 --> 00:05:34.887
I'll start filming soon.

00:05:34.887 --> 00:05:36.826
Oh, I just found out that
they're doing a Chevrolet

00:05:36.826 --> 00:05:38.884
auto show here, so they're blocking out

00:05:38.884 --> 00:05:40.566
Yonge-Dundas Square.

00:05:40.566 --> 00:05:41.726
That's why no one's around.

00:05:41.726 --> 00:05:44.357
So I also can't film there, either.

00:05:44.357 --> 00:05:47.092
I'm going to walk down the street

00:05:47.092 --> 00:05:48.897
and Probably go to Queen Street West,

00:05:48.897 --> 00:05:52.264
which is another really busy
part of downtown Toronto,

00:05:52.264 --> 00:05:54.322
so I'm going to try doing that

00:05:54.322 --> 00:05:56.713
and yeah, you know, life happens.

00:05:56.713 --> 00:05:57.998
You got to adjust.

00:05:57.998 --> 00:05:59.231
You got to adjust

00:05:59.231 --> 00:06:03.106
to when things don't
go exactly as planned.

00:06:03.106 --> 00:06:05.972
So we'll see, we'll see, we'll see.

00:06:05.972 --> 00:06:08.393
Everything, every
opportunity is an opportunity

00:06:08.393 --> 00:06:09.542
to learn, guys.

00:06:09.542 --> 00:06:10.761
All the time.

00:06:10.761 --> 00:06:14.094
(acoustic guitar music)

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:17.714
All right, I found a busier place.

00:06:17.714 --> 00:06:20.705
I'm actually at the Toronto Civic Center,

00:06:20.705 --> 00:06:22.294
I believe it's called.

00:06:22.294 --> 00:06:25.963
This is where we hold all our events

00:06:25.963 --> 00:06:28.375
and there's different
exhibits going on right now.

00:06:28.375 --> 00:06:29.980
Lots of people around.

00:06:29.980 --> 00:06:32.112
Not as much as I would like.

00:06:32.112 --> 00:06:33.553
I don't know what I was expecting.

00:06:33.553 --> 00:06:35.518
I think when I wanted to do this event,

00:06:35.518 --> 00:06:37.697
I pictured thousands of people around me,

00:06:37.697 --> 00:06:39.318
but I don't know.

00:06:39.318 --> 00:06:40.435
Maybe this is how busy it always is.

00:06:40.435 --> 00:06:42.134
I all made it up in my head,

00:06:42.134 --> 00:06:43.798
that it's supposed to be like, busier.

00:06:43.798 --> 00:06:45.256
Anyway, so, it looks like

00:06:45.256 --> 00:06:46.849
they're going to have a concert soon,

00:06:46.849 --> 00:06:50.258
so kind of give you a glimpse
of how it looks like here.

00:06:50.258 --> 00:06:52.270
There's a food truck there.

00:06:52.270 --> 00:06:53.775
Oh, look!

00:06:53.775 --> 00:06:56.450
There's our beautiful Toronto,

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:58.796
Toronto sign right there.

00:06:58.796 --> 00:07:00.928
Okay, so I'm going to try
to find a little place

00:07:00.928 --> 00:07:03.737
to set up my tripod
because I lost my big one.

00:07:03.737 --> 00:07:06.320
And yeah, it's going to happen.

00:07:07.429 --> 00:07:08.853
Testing, testing, testing.

00:07:08.853 --> 00:07:11.930
Since I'm here at (laughs).

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:14.138
My first attempt in shooting,

00:07:14.138 --> 00:07:17.335
I realized that I'm a
little bit too far away

00:07:17.335 --> 00:07:20.656
from the action of Civic Center.

00:07:20.656 --> 00:07:23.202
And primarily because I
couldn't find anything

00:07:23.202 --> 00:07:25.874
to put my tripod on, so I
have to use my creativity

00:07:25.874 --> 00:07:29.154
to go right in the
middle of all the action.

00:07:29.154 --> 00:07:30.208
Yeah, yeah.

00:07:30.208 --> 00:07:31.492
That's the point of all of this.

00:07:31.492 --> 00:07:34.308
The point of all of this
is for me to face my fear

00:07:34.308 --> 00:07:35.881
of being around a lot of people

00:07:35.881 --> 00:07:37.151
and I was kind of far away from people,

00:07:37.151 --> 00:07:38.851
so it's a good check in for myself.

00:07:38.851 --> 00:07:41.510
Yeah, let me go find some place.

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:43.771
So I found a busier place to set up,

00:07:43.771 --> 00:07:46.102
but the only thing is, there was no place

00:07:46.102 --> 00:07:48.118
for me to set up my tripod (laughs).

00:07:48.118 --> 00:07:52.802
So I have the tripod on
a bench and I'm sitting

00:07:52.802 --> 00:07:55.914
on the floor, which kind of
adds to the awkwardness of this,

00:07:55.914 --> 00:07:58.013
which is great because
that's what I'm looking for

00:07:58.013 --> 00:08:00.540
and I think people are
probably wondering why

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:03.787
I'm sitting on the floor
and recording, but hey,

00:08:03.787 --> 00:08:05.298
that's part of the challenge.

00:08:05.298 --> 00:08:07.478
(upbeat music)

00:08:07.478 --> 00:08:09.979
Hey everyone, so as I'm
here, downtown Toronto,

00:08:09.979 --> 00:08:13.577
facing my fear in filming in public,

00:08:13.577 --> 00:08:14.908
I thought I'd share some tips

00:08:14.908 --> 00:08:16.478
in how to overcome your fear,

00:08:16.478 --> 00:08:17.988
or at least push through it.

00:08:17.988 --> 00:08:20.376
The number one thing to always think about

00:08:20.376 --> 00:08:23.179
is how is your fear holding you back?

00:08:23.179 --> 00:08:25.369
So for example, I want to be a speaker

00:08:25.369 --> 00:08:27.574
and I'm going to be in
situations where I'm speaking

00:08:27.574 --> 00:08:29.840
in front of many people

00:08:29.840 --> 00:08:32.003
that I have never met.

00:08:32.003 --> 00:08:33.859
I have no idea if they
care about me, like me,

00:08:33.859 --> 00:08:37.276
or if they hate everything I have to say,

00:08:38.184 --> 00:08:39.356
so I have to overcome that.

00:08:39.356 --> 00:08:41.831
I'm not always going to have the comfort

00:08:41.831 --> 00:08:45.332
of my own backyard, filming
where everything is safe

00:08:45.332 --> 00:08:47.189
and it's my home and nobody else

00:08:47.189 --> 00:08:49.332
is looking at me, or have the comfort

00:08:49.332 --> 00:08:52.465
in going to the TDS studio
where it's only Evan

00:08:52.465 --> 00:08:56.064
and our camera person, so
I needed to push through

00:08:56.064 --> 00:08:58.789
that fear in thinking that
how it's been holding me back

00:08:58.789 --> 00:09:02.903
all my life really helped
me go through this process

00:09:02.903 --> 00:09:06.304
and really, kind of diminished
all the fear that I had

00:09:06.304 --> 00:09:08.151
in filming in public.

00:09:08.151 --> 00:09:10.940
Now that I'm here, it's
actually not that bad.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:14.399
I don't feel that anxiety
anymore that I used to.

00:09:14.399 --> 00:09:15.232
It was.

00:09:17.604 --> 00:09:19.846
(laughs)

00:09:19.846 --> 00:09:21.281
(mutters)

00:09:21.281 --> 00:09:23.886
It's mostly all in my head

00:09:23.886 --> 00:09:27.599
and when you're there,
it's actually not that bad.

00:09:27.599 --> 00:09:30.345
The number two thing that
you want to think about

00:09:30.345 --> 00:09:32.358
is to start small.

00:09:32.358 --> 00:09:35.315
You don't want to go
from like, being like,

00:09:35.315 --> 00:09:37.457
completely petrified and doing something

00:09:37.457 --> 00:09:40.246
and then completely flooding
your system and going crazy.

00:09:40.246 --> 00:09:43.519
So for me, I had a fear
in filming in public,

00:09:43.519 --> 00:09:47.699
so I started off filming while
I was walking on a sidewalk.

00:09:47.699 --> 00:09:50.904
Then I started filming in a grocery store,

00:09:50.904 --> 00:09:54.763
and then I started filming
where my class was going on.

00:09:54.763 --> 00:09:58.758
And little by little, it kind
of helped me build up muscle

00:09:58.758 --> 00:10:03.147
to face my biggest fear, which
is coming here, downtown,

00:10:03.147 --> 00:10:05.513
and filming in front of
all these people around me,

00:10:05.513 --> 00:10:07.900
and that really, really helped.

00:10:07.900 --> 00:10:10.050
So when you want to think about it, like,

00:10:10.050 --> 00:10:11.647
if you have a fear of swimming,

00:10:11.647 --> 00:10:13.570
maybe you want to try
out in your bathtub first

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:16.367
and then go to a shallow end of a pool

00:10:16.367 --> 00:10:19.742
and then, later on, you could
go to a deep end of a pool.

00:10:19.742 --> 00:10:22.327
So little by little, you're
going to train yourself

00:10:22.327 --> 00:10:23.899
to overcome that fear.

00:10:23.899 --> 00:10:26.745
And number three is to keep pushing!

00:10:26.745 --> 00:10:29.965
Just because you've conquered
one fear doesn't mean

00:10:29.965 --> 00:10:31.574
that you're going to stop there.

00:10:31.574 --> 00:10:33.194
So for me, I've conquered this fear

00:10:33.194 --> 00:10:35.651
in filming in public.

00:10:35.651 --> 00:10:37.628
It doesn't really feel
like a fear anymore,

00:10:37.628 --> 00:10:39.805
so now I need to think
about what's next for me

00:10:39.805 --> 00:10:42.422
and keep pushing through,
and not be content

00:10:42.422 --> 00:10:44.610
that I, mean, yes.

00:10:44.610 --> 00:10:46.071
I'm happy that I overcame this fear,

00:10:46.071 --> 00:10:47.826
but I need to keep going through.

00:10:47.826 --> 00:10:49.774
So I think the next thing I want to do

00:10:49.774 --> 00:10:53.941
is go on a big stage and speak
in front of a lot of people.

00:10:55.552 --> 00:10:56.385
A lot.

00:10:57.707 --> 00:10:58.748
Hundreds of people.

00:10:58.748 --> 00:11:01.831
That's what I would like to do, yeah.

00:11:02.879 --> 00:11:04.160
So I finished filming
my little piece (laughs)

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:05.987
by setting up on the bench.

00:11:05.987 --> 00:11:07.353
It was interesting.

00:11:07.353 --> 00:11:08.681
It was good.

00:11:08.681 --> 00:11:11.879
I mean, I had to do what
I could with the situation

00:11:11.879 --> 00:11:13.142
I was in.

00:11:13.142 --> 00:11:15.655
I can't believe I left my
tripod in my husband's car,

00:11:15.655 --> 00:11:20.566
but I had to use my creativity
to kind of maneuver.

00:11:20.566 --> 00:11:21.536
Maneuver?

00:11:21.536 --> 00:11:23.707
Is maneuver the right word, or is it?

00:11:23.707 --> 00:11:24.723
Oh, manure?

00:11:24.723 --> 00:11:25.723
Okay anyways, that's
not the point (laughs).

00:11:25.723 --> 00:11:28.223
Maneuver around the obstacles.

00:11:29.239 --> 00:11:32.739
But more importantly, it's beautiful here!

00:11:34.194 --> 00:11:35.510
I used to live downtown.

00:11:35.510 --> 00:11:37.911
I lived downtown Toronto
for about six years

00:11:37.911 --> 00:11:41.133
before moving up north,
and I love it here.

00:11:41.133 --> 00:11:43.512
The energy is so vibrant.

00:11:43.512 --> 00:11:44.720
The people are so wonderful

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:46.351
and everyone's so diverse

00:11:46.351 --> 00:11:47.982
and there's always something going on.

00:11:47.982 --> 00:11:51.390
So that part, I really miss
about living in the city.

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:54.355
I'm going to take a walk
around and look at this exhibit

00:11:54.355 --> 00:11:56.129
that's going on.

00:11:56.129 --> 00:11:58.553
It's called "No Blank Brain Project,"

00:11:58.553 --> 00:12:00.603
so I'm going to take a look
and then I'm going to head home

00:12:00.603 --> 00:12:02.436
and go see my husband.

00:12:03.672 --> 00:12:06.255
(upbeat music)

00:12:12.445 --> 00:12:14.494
Okay, so I'm back at Union Station.

00:12:14.494 --> 00:12:16.038
It's so interesting here.

00:12:16.038 --> 00:12:17.563
There's lot of stuff going on.

00:12:17.563 --> 00:12:20.258
Anyway, I have about half-an-hour to kill,

00:12:20.258 --> 00:12:23.274
so I'm going to get online and answer

00:12:23.274 --> 00:12:27.129
some of your comments because
my Unlocking Lily episode six.

00:12:27.129 --> 00:12:28.568
No, five.

00:12:28.568 --> 00:12:29.614
Five (laughs).

00:12:29.614 --> 00:12:31.592
Five just came out.

00:12:31.592 --> 00:12:33.984
Yeah, I'm excited to
see what you guys wrote.

00:12:33.984 --> 00:12:36.567
(upbeat music)

00:12:42.058 --> 00:12:43.520
Just got off the train.

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:45.129
Going to go see the husband.

00:12:45.129 --> 00:12:47.624
Look at how beautiful it is.

00:12:47.624 --> 00:12:49.012
Isn't that just nice?

00:12:49.012 --> 00:12:50.415
Yeah.

00:12:50.415 --> 00:12:53.533
What a change of scenery
from crazy downtown Toronto

00:12:53.533 --> 00:12:55.140
to farmland.

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:56.227
Beauty!

00:12:56.227 --> 00:12:57.613
Look who I found!

00:12:57.613 --> 00:12:58.612
- Hello.
- It's my husband.

00:12:58.612 --> 00:12:59.859
- Hello, everyone.
- Are you happy to see me?

00:12:59.859 --> 00:13:01.077
- Oh yeah.
- Yeah.

00:13:01.077 --> 00:13:02.102
- I'm happy to see you,

00:13:02.102 --> 00:13:03.798
happy to see you, too.
(Lily laughs)

00:13:03.798 --> 00:13:07.797
- So I just got back from
filming in public, guys (laughs)

00:13:07.797 --> 00:13:10.130
and it was not nearly as bad

00:13:12.272 --> 00:13:15.189
as I thought it would be initially.

00:13:16.541 --> 00:13:17.847
I was like, playing up all these
scenarios leading up to it.

00:13:17.847 --> 00:13:19.370
What if people stare at me weird?

00:13:19.370 --> 00:13:22.453
What if I accidentally drop my phone?

00:13:23.416 --> 00:13:25.431
What if people judge me?

00:13:25.431 --> 00:13:27.041
What if people say things to me?

00:13:27.041 --> 00:13:29.291
And honestly, no one cared.

00:13:31.543 --> 00:13:33.539
Everyone was going along their merry way.

00:13:33.539 --> 00:13:35.167
Everything was fine.

00:13:35.167 --> 00:13:36.957
People were having a great time.

00:13:36.957 --> 00:13:39.347
I think some people did kind of look over,

00:13:39.347 --> 00:13:42.576
but you know, it was out of curiosity

00:13:42.576 --> 00:13:44.779
and not like, sheer judgment.

00:13:44.779 --> 00:13:45.763
Maybe they were judging, I don't know,

00:13:45.763 --> 00:13:47.559
but I felt great about it.

00:13:47.559 --> 00:13:50.689
I was so happy to be there,
downtown in the midst

00:13:50.689 --> 00:13:52.173
of all the action.

00:13:52.173 --> 00:13:54.455
I did have a few obstacles
that I did have to

00:13:54.455 --> 00:13:57.210
kind of use my creativity
to kind of work around,

00:13:57.210 --> 00:13:59.084
but it all worked out in the end

00:13:59.084 --> 00:14:02.199
and that goes to show
that fear is sometimes

00:14:02.199 --> 00:14:06.216
just in your head, and when
you go out there and do it,

00:14:06.216 --> 00:14:08.996
it's not as bad as you thought originally,

00:14:08.996 --> 00:14:11.096
which brings me to the next point.

00:14:11.096 --> 00:14:14.888
So the question of the day
is, what is your biggest fear

00:14:14.888 --> 00:14:17.282
that you still have yet to overcome?

00:14:17.282 --> 00:14:19.197
Write in the comments below

00:14:19.197 --> 00:14:21.017
and I'll join in on the discussion.

00:14:21.017 --> 00:14:23.476
So for my next challenge,
I'm going to go to an event

00:14:23.476 --> 00:14:25.309
and start with my why.

00:14:26.419 --> 00:14:28.601
Because I learned from Simon Sinek,

00:14:28.601 --> 00:14:31.661
instead of going with what
you do and how you do it,

00:14:31.661 --> 00:14:33.710
you need to start with why.

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:36.695
So thank you so much for
watching and I really hope

00:14:36.695 --> 00:14:39.213
you enjoyed my journey
throughout downtown Toronto.

00:14:39.213 --> 00:14:41.564
It was a lot fun for me

00:14:41.564 --> 00:14:44.276
and I actually have a special
shout-out for Halona Black.

00:14:44.276 --> 00:14:47.679
So Halona Black wrote, "How exciting!

00:14:47.679 --> 00:14:50.181
"It's great to have a mentor
who can push you to do

00:14:50.181 --> 00:14:53.006
"things that you may not feel ready for.

00:14:53.006 --> 00:14:56.256
"I need to do more of this for myself."

00:14:57.235 --> 00:14:58.424
Yes, Halona Black, it is true.

00:14:58.424 --> 00:15:02.007
I do have a bomb of a mentor, Evan

00:15:02.007 --> 00:15:05.997
and he is so wonderful, and he unleashes

00:15:05.997 --> 00:15:09.035
all sorts of belief on me
(laughs) when I need it

00:15:09.035 --> 00:15:12.315
the most and I wouldn't be
able to do a lot of the things

00:15:12.315 --> 00:15:15.270
I have done recently if it wasn't for him.

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:18.005
So, so, so thankful for the lovely Evan.

00:15:18.005 --> 00:15:21.138
So when I first started
out on this series,

00:15:21.138 --> 00:15:23.690
I thought it was just a
way to document my journey

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:25.923
and show some transparency
to you guys as well,

00:15:25.923 --> 00:15:30.401
but I had no idea that it
would be inspiring for you

00:15:30.401 --> 00:15:32.790
and it would inspire you to do the things

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:33.851
that you want to do.

00:15:33.851 --> 00:15:37.587
And I am completely at a loss of words

00:15:37.587 --> 00:15:40.028
of all the wonderful comments
that have been pouring in.

00:15:40.028 --> 00:15:44.144
I can't thank you enough
and be grateful enough

00:15:44.144 --> 00:15:47.339
and I really do hope that one day,

00:15:47.339 --> 00:15:50.844
I'll be able to meet all of you in person.

00:15:50.844 --> 00:15:54.866
But if I don't, it makes me
feel good that we're all in this

00:15:54.866 --> 00:15:58.038
together and we're going
on this journey arm-in-arm.

00:15:58.038 --> 00:15:59.626
Thank you.

00:15:59.626 --> 00:16:01.475
Thank you, thank you so much

00:16:01.475 --> 00:16:04.808
and I will see you guys very, very soon.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:09.127
(loud explosion)

